  "scenario": {
    "description": "Canonical EvidenceForge iteration-test scenario for fast generate/evaluate/fix cycles. It\npreserves the expanded environment and attack narrative while including authored,\ntransport-correlated IDS assertions, sensor-local filtering, cross-platform SMB activity,\na second domain controller, centralized monitoring, and deliberate no-alert cases for broad\nautomated and LLM-as-a-judge quality evaluation.\nMeridian Healthcare Solutions is a mid-size healthcare IT company providing EHR\nintegration services from a corporate HQ with an on-premises data center. The\nstoryline compresses an APT-style web-app intrusion, Linux and Windows lateral\nmovement, credential theft, domain compromise, C2, DNS tunneling, data staging,\nexfiltration, email abuse, and cleanup into a 6-hour collection window while\npreserving broad event-type and log-format coverage. This expanded variant adds\nexplicit on-prem email topology, SMTP routing, corpus-backed message bodies,\nMIME artifacts, distribution groups, Bcc handling, STARTTLS visibility, ISP relay\negress, inbound/outbound/internal mail, explicit mailbox reads, rejected mail,\nand deterministic background email traffic. This benchmark epoch also adds one\nrepresentative benign cleartext multipart support upload through the explicit proxy.\nThis separate epoch adds two macOS 27 arm64 engineering workstations and substantial\nlocal-terminal, GUI, browser-helper, SSH and explicit system-job activity. The original\nsix-hour mixed-fleet workload is retained; its date moves to a supported Mac epoch.\n",
